  "targets": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0028",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p105-04882-s004",
      "sentenceText": "Researchers measure how many candidates from a set pool you interview before deciding to hire a particular individual.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7cfa58636312ba085d506670ad3c9eb6d386b594d92966cfccd00bc3b85c5278",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p105-04882-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-013",
      "parentFingerprint": "7acf48a34556cbada096158e29e6011bbaa265a847ad20a495ce3421511cef6a",
      "passageSha256": "669c07c00e1c0b53fcbeb61f4e7ce6b279e820e369fef9564bb9d28d84e8d02d",
      "pdfPages": [
        105
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0029",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p105-04882-s005",
      "sentenceText": "You cannot go back to previous interviewees, and you must make binary decisions (yes or no) until you make a yes (hire) decision.",
      "sentenceSha256": "e5752a43827da683b185739bab0203e939dd76b01cb723783edfe7454814e563",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p105-04882-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-014",
      "parentFingerprint": "469925062e4b6e6ee3364f779c53c9b64453fd00285f6d9f476fbdd656eb78b3",
      "passageSha256": "306350bc07b1ba7eaba6693957132400e50753dd9fa728a2f694aa8e23b4277c",
      "pdfPages": [
        105
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 3,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0030",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p105-04882-s007",
      "sentenceText": "This is called the “37 percent rule.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "7c7e8cc864c7f846889695e38d2ba6d1d039955ecb07bf56e1c41003bf6a999d",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p105-04882-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-014",
      "parentFingerprint": "469925062e4b6e6ee3364f779c53c9b64453fd00285f6d9f476fbdd656eb78b3",
      "passageSha256": "306350bc07b1ba7eaba6693957132400e50753dd9fa728a2f694aa8e23b4277c",
      "pdfPages": [
        105
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 4,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0031",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p105-04882-s008",
      "sentenceText": "How many people actually follow the 37 percent rule?",
      "sentenceSha256": "8bf46cb0f9e095996fbec3ee0b206486ac0116708b50db17f4df77d5e38f49d7",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p105-04882-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-014",
      "parentFingerprint": "469925062e4b6e6ee3364f779c53c9b64453fd00285f6d9f476fbdd656eb78b3",
      "passageSha256": "306350bc07b1ba7eaba6693957132400e50753dd9fa728a2f694aa8e23b4277c",
      "pdfPages": [
        105
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 5,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0032",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p106-00750-s001",
      "sentenceText": "If you had 100 potential mates, would you date 37 of them at least once and then start using the 37 percent rule until you find the best available one?",
      "sentenceSha256": "52f5dc693f91f80ca7a77d013852965a4d4d06bc7d7b14bc66ced92694a9fae4",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p106-00750-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-016",
      "parentFingerprint": "bae67303d0da71bc38cd414dbce0e248f1d8457db5b39a565b2e030cd5ec2c62",
      "passageSha256": "d6c2bb0823f91d3d2254f282a1c61c60fb66c8f752c32b116232dcffeb24b7bd",
      "pdfPages": [
        106
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 6,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0033",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p106-00750-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Probably not.",
      "sentenceSha256": "65e33c1f33c53959f172d852d00014d02d6fa33cbb820e16b20d6a947f8e37bd",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p106-00750-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-016",
      "parentFingerprint": "bae67303d0da71bc38cd414dbce0e248f1d8457db5b39a565b2e030cd5ec2c62",
      "passageSha256": "d6c2bb0823f91d3d2254f282a1c61c60fb66c8f752c32b116232dcffeb24b7bd",
      "pdfPages": [
        106
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 7,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0034",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p106-00750-s005",
      "sentenceText": "Then your extensive search would be wasted.",
      "sentenceSha256": "0101edb46a473a1300f6f2b6f998fa157b55cb39517f958cf9e068ae9eb43acc",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p106-00750-r005-006",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-017",
      "parentFingerprint": "7f86852e5f1c09e80c9caa55444afd9988bc8b190beae7f0a6f99150cb8585b8",
      "passageSha256": "bdb1c02db232f8294ed560259c5d0bbffdfe68ea102d5391a9382c00fb0a2b07",
      "pdfPages": [
        106
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 8,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0035",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p106-02115-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Nevertheless, it is interesting to know that psychologists have conducted a lot of secretary problem (SP) experiments that minimize additional search costs (e.g., just flipping another card instead of finding a time and location to meet a date).",
      "sentenceSha256": "813ec74d05bfdd3a69fdd95bb0fa170917f577447a72da683a6399e60b9418ea",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p106-02115-r001-002",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-018",
      "parentFingerprint": "52a543835ddead2df4fe1a08e1c1e0eefaef78ce2ef9d75d28265d1e860f0bf8",
      "passageSha256": "bee69e65029d85ac2a4703467d2f99a8b40d39b96c92353c97fbbe7df9786227",
      "pdfPages": [
        106
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 9,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0036",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p106-02115-s003",
      "sentenceText": "For instance, only 30 percent of college students followed the 37 percent rule under experimental conditions, though college students were slightly better than pigeons, of which only 17 percent followed the rule.",
      "sentenceSha256": "dd73f0f078a23192c57aaabb28ad492a465ba4129010eefefcb3e5430f29bfe2",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p106-02115-r003-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-019",
      "parentFingerprint": "a065d338824f00f4acdf732e0e2d70cf4edd1514e226772d5280bf5d52914051",
      "passageSha256": "6cfe6288dfc1734c98fca0cd0c9d6674dd1105e521804dbe99456f2720d63687",
      "pdfPages": [
        106
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 10,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0037",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p106-02115-s004",
      "sentenceText": "Herbranson and colleagues concluded as follows: “Across three experiments, pigeons and humans failed to consistently use the optimal solution to the SP.",
      "sentenceSha256": "91b06d86788a77b644aea56f1ebba1e469c04ef84f1450eb53d1f6f97ed1cadb",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p106-02115-r003-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-019",
      "parentFingerprint": "a065d338824f00f4acdf732e0e2d70cf4edd1514e226772d5280bf5d52914051",
      "passageSha256": "6cfe6288dfc1734c98fca0cd0c9d6674dd1105e521804dbe99456f2720d63687",
      "pdfPages": [
        106
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 11,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0038",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p106-04455-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Indeed, economists argue that people make suboptimal choices in mate selection because they do not explore enough.",
      "sentenceSha256": "e6e8bb3d3d4c78bdc446e8676141a025943c467f061ff099b677e54bd9d4ead1",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p106-04455-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-020",
      "parentFingerprint": "e77df48922b17ad671aa6b4b7d88d317ba738607956b7b429012ff5009bbaa12",
      "passageSha256": "844aa416d22b5187d7f3d063b5975d0a8e361b868b79db6a7e83532823a63991",
      "pdfPages": [
        106
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0039",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s02-p106-04455-s003",
      "sentenceText": "For most people, the more exploration they do, the better choices they make.",
      "sentenceSha256": "959bbc155ff2545c8f2732781d80782551e96ced9bc2c82e3aa48d2ce5e810f4",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s02-p106-04455-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-020",
      "parentFingerprint": "e77df48922b17ad671aa6b4b7d88d317ba738607956b7b429012ff5009bbaa12",
      "passageSha256": "844aa416d22b5187d7f3d063b5975d0a8e361b868b79db6a7e83532823a63991",
      "pdfPages": [
        106
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0040",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Psychologists Samantha Cohen and Peter Todd analyzed nationally representative data collected by the Centers for Disease Control to gain insight into the exploration-exploitation trade-off in real marital decisions.",
      "sentenceSha256": "180a18be7134aac2a56d32df2e2416cb35b617afb9a8c8abc0845667342de2f4",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-021",
      "parentFingerprint": "d17e5afc46723c597bdcd6d82f15ac8e56451782588dc5b45b5facaa4c858444",
      "passageSha256": "e626a75bebb282fa34b17046605ef5f543bd9f40c8f29ef882c231ea44dbdfd9",
      "pdfPages": [
        106,
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0041",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-s002",
      "sentenceText": "They learned that some people spend a long time dating several people before getting married, whereas others spend a short time dating a few and settle down quickly.",
      "sentenceSha256": "d6ed7dd2e419a099f4b5f30ac0236b6e761a94585e544916cc02a7d9291ca39b",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-021",
      "parentFingerprint": "d17e5afc46723c597bdcd6d82f15ac8e56451782588dc5b45b5facaa4c858444",
      "passageSha256": "e626a75bebb282fa34b17046605ef5f543bd9f40c8f29ef882c231ea44dbdfd9",
      "pdfPages": [
        106,
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 15,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0042",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-s004",
      "sentenceText": "The animal behavior literature and computer simulations both suggest that insufficient exploration results in more errors.",
      "sentenceSha256": "2af47afed1f280ad2d38958a87d8f26ad8c079b300d9f8e6d8f893b3b60627a1",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-r004-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-022",
      "parentFingerprint": "e7b1583ea0013bf249816f1e036ee2bcbd56b11656d0af84ee4e6ee73076d1e4",
      "passageSha256": "4aeea1fbfc26c72552211a246e4f042f7a77836dabe5a5bfdf258140a8460b85",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 16,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0043",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-s005",
      "sentenceText": "Of course, if one mate were far better than the rest, there would be no need to explore—the choice would be obvious.",
      "sentenceSha256": "896407e11d7607b568a9ac00ff88b7f1f0a652c61632057ae0df77dbf652a603",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-r004-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-022",
      "parentFingerprint": "e7b1583ea0013bf249816f1e036ee2bcbd56b11656d0af84ee4e6ee73076d1e4",
      "passageSha256": "4aeea1fbfc26c72552211a246e4f042f7a77836dabe5a5bfdf258140a8460b85",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 17,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0044",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-s007",
      "sentenceText": "This means that it is better to explore more before settling down on one mate.",
      "sentenceSha256": "15652b1e591ef386dd442034d8b090c235525e68f96007e7dd2bcd533114ef57",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-r004-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-022",
      "parentFingerprint": "e7b1583ea0013bf249816f1e036ee2bcbd56b11656d0af84ee4e6ee73076d1e4",
      "passageSha256": "4aeea1fbfc26c72552211a246e4f042f7a77836dabe5a5bfdf258140a8460b85",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 18,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0045",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-s009",
      "sentenceText": "So, on average, the more exploration, the more marital stability.",
      "sentenceSha256": "3c46e0f7e4d66c898771c3c7f28d37319239560e7d5018409a9c58d9716a25a5",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p106-06135-r008-009",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-023",
      "parentFingerprint": "7df1e69ea58df3190c2a96e0bbec1e6e9ceb111baa06da58f64124b13fa50d5f",
      "passageSha256": "2be473969a0be922eb4b0a5fc612bc9f8a2834081ce3c65d334f4c6acca97ba7",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 19,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0046",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-s001",
      "sentenceText": "The CDC data are consistent with the 37 percent rule.",
      "sentenceSha256": "f6b27a0a76c77f2665a3666221502db8e75825763baf42df22ddc7536694ef85",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-024",
      "parentFingerprint": "9f0d8718b43b7179a81f3ecd43cd8d77773966c2439876d29ee637e5ed4fcffc",
      "passageSha256": "eeeac3dffa5721cb8a08ca9c4b190d2d0e4489b875a8e7238a79425a35893b2c",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 20,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0047",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-s002",
      "sentenceText": "However, Peter Todd and Geoffrey Miller take issue with the 37 percent rule on several grounds.",
      "sentenceSha256": "fb195da46527bef9a21e09130b42d5190c99c6c7af18761a0498634533a2f729",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-024",
      "parentFingerprint": "9f0d8718b43b7179a81f3ecd43cd8d77773966c2439876d29ee637e5ed4fcffc",
      "passageSha256": "eeeac3dffa5721cb8a08ca9c4b190d2d0e4489b875a8e7238a79425a35893b2c",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 21,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0048",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-s005",
      "sentenceText": "Rather, being able to find one of the best options is (e.g., the top 10 percent).",
      "sentenceSha256": "62a0162a7b62f242b0823d37c8fb2d40c29b9dd3a976c9a4b479aca0acaff3df",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-025",
      "parentFingerprint": "ecb16e572083ce4b96d8fa5e672b86dbbcecea8d7e834f2179bfdbc5b5e1afdf",
      "passageSha256": "4391165c9ce9b206d4471d75cc1fba43c725dfdb9b5ec9f89396af62a84cf467",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 22,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0049",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-s008",
      "sentenceText": "When the number of potential mates is set to 1,000, an even more cursory search of just 3 percent yields the highest probability of finding someone from the top 10 percent.",
      "sentenceSha256": "5e2e5e63c6140804ce302d9cbb7432ddc095b11f27d58f380e7fb566fffbc9c6",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-r008-009",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-026",
      "parentFingerprint": "da31547818f585d67c50463992701b4a0d73036e5a345b1a7d5abf243ad02a7c",
      "passageSha256": "9cd24fc3b830a5ea4eb594c3bf60a2c1bbec7bb6d3c4ddc94d15d1ec05dbc8ff",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 23,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0050",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-s011",
      "sentenceText": "A lot more reasonable than the 37 percent rule.",
      "sentenceSha256": "d968c89ce0aaae4dfd67d71bfcfc101473ecff82ef8383967a2f41ded9c362df",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p107-03285-r010-011",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-027",
      "parentFingerprint": "61139ba116d3701e3b9baa4fe8a3f17258656d84725482f5f926f3540d24b1ca",
      "passageSha256": "292e76c9f017115de81e1083be2232c021370e478c900b189b30a3624cb30cf8",
      "pdfPages": [
        107
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 24,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0051",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p107-06600-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In the end, Todd and Miller argue that the “take a dozen” heuristic, regardless of the problem set, does a pretty good job of finding a top 10 percent option.",
      "sentenceSha256": "3428f527b08d1486b48d3dc57e96234eb1c261f7d607e9e381882c1bd26e021e",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p107-06600-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-028",
      "parentFingerprint": "6b7d3ed7b95f06b59d5db2b5d2d2380d7507b472232e989ef16292b71424beb2",
      "passageSha256": "82aed2bbd9ea1b7885125ffbfad9e7fbd04de9e6b5ce59550e1388e7973b28bf",
      "pdfPages": [
        107,
        108
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 25,
      "questionId": "qe-c10-0052",
      "sentenceId": "c10-s03-p107-06600-s002",
      "sentenceText": "This means when you next look for a new romantic partner or a new apartment, you had better consider at least a dozen before making a decision.",
      "sentenceSha256": "3405820ea76ce79a604a71721719a03cc732f77872c8c0d08001ea2ce4e1be05",
      "readingUnitId": "c10-s03-p107-06600-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c10-028",
      "parentFingerprint": "6b7d3ed7b95f06b59d5db2b5d2d2380d7507b472232e989ef16292b71424beb2",
      "passageSha256": "82aed2bbd9ea1b7885125ffbfad9e7fbd04de9e6b5ce59550e1388e7973b28bf",
      "pdfPages": [
        107,
